   The author performed a branch-and-bound search over 3-free sets mod b
for each b ≤ 158 in an attempt to find Kempner sets which outperformed the
greedy set G3 = K({0, 1}, 3) + 1. This search was unsuccessful, indicating
that G3 is an influential local maximum and that larger search spaces will
be needed to improve lower bounds on M3 .
   To extend these results to larger b, at least conditionally, the author ran
searches with additional heuristic pruning. Two methods were considered:
   P1. One asserts an upper bound on #S and reruns any search in which
       the upper bound was realized.
   P2. One restricts to 3-free sets which deviate from a greedy construction
       for 3-free sets mod b a bounded number of times.
In addition to the unconditional search over b ≤ 158, the author ran searches
under (P1) for b ∈ [159, 316] and under (P1) and (P2) for b ∈ [317, 400].
These searches, which ran for a total of 8679 core-hours (at 2.3 GHz), were
unsuccessful in improving G3 . The largest harmonic sums found associated
