codex
The full paper changes the triage picture: it does not present a hard “find a progression” task. Its nontrivial search is Section 3’s branch-and-bound search for large subsets of residues containing no modular \(k\)-term progression; Theorem 1.2 then turns such a digit set into an infinite progression-free Kempner set. I’m checking whether that search can be inverse-generated without giving away the planted digit set, and whether the paper’s explicit/easy constructions disqualify it.
